{"full_name":"JayPokale/Chisle","path":"README.md","fetched_at":"2026-11-23T21:30:07.264Z","length":12116,"text":"English &middot; Español &middot; 한국어 &middot; 简体中文 &middot; 日本語 \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n Shorter answers than caveman and ponytail. No accuracy lost. \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n See both answers \n \n\nThe prompt: \"Implement an order state machine covering created, paid, shipped, delivered, cancelled and refunded, with the legal transitions enforced and invalid ones rejected.\" Excerpts from the verbatim committed answers in raw-314-direct/large-s2 :\n\n \n no ruleset: 132 lines, 1,307 answer tokens Chisle: 60 lines, 577 answer tokens \n \n\n \n\n…plus a StateTransition class nothing uses, example usage and tests, and \"Key Design Decisions\", \"Why these transitions\" and \"Features\" sections.\n\n \n\n \n\nThen a short example and a five-line list of the transitions.\n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n Every raw transcript is committed, losses included. Method and data · why we publish the losses \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n Other ways to install \n \n\n \n\n \n\nPer-agent setup, upgrading and config: docs/usage.md.\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n ⭐ Star the repo : it costs zero tokens. · Follow @JayPokale for more tools. \n\n \n \n \n\n MIT · Contributing · Began as a merge of caveman and ponytail ( notices ) · Command filters follow RTK 's design","intro":{"html":"<h4>\n  \n    \n    <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JayPokale/Chisle/main/assets/readme/banner-light.svg\" alt=\"Chisle: fewer tokens in, fewer tokens out, same answers.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"100%\" />\n  \n</h4><p>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/JayPokale/Chisle/stargazers\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" 